1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,434
This horror demo shipped with
two AI agent runtimes inside it.

2
00:00:04,684 --> 00:00:09,954
Not one. Two. Plus a tokenizer,
in a game about a haunted fort.

3
00:00:13,804 --> 00:00:23,672
Rudravati is a first-person supernatural horror set in the ruins of an Indian fort.
You go looking for your brother. The fort has opinions about that.

4
00:00:23,922 --> 00:00:29,532
It's made by LeZit Games, who also publish it.
English and Hindi, both with full voice acting.

5
00:00:35,782 --> 00:00:42,489
The demo went up yesterday. It has no reviews yet,
and single digits of players. This one is all build.

6
00:00:42,739 --> 00:00:50,256
Before the files, one thing the store won't tell you.
Steam's own database still lists the parent game under a different name.

7
00:00:50,506 --> 00:01:05,572
It was Ratnavati, Curse of Bhangarh. Bhangarh Fort is a real place in Rajasthan, and Ratnavati is the princess in its legend.
The store now says Rudravati, Curse of Bhankilla. Both names were changed to invented ones.

8
00:01:05,822 --> 00:01:11,562
The executable is still called RUDRAVATI.
Why they changed it, a manifest can't tell you.

9
00:01:11,812 --> 00:01:17,239
Now the build. Six point zero nine gigabytes,
two hundred and twenty eight files.

10
00:01:17,489 --> 00:01:24,849
It's Unity, on the High Definition render pipeline,
with Unity 6's GPU resident drawer and ray tracing.

11
00:01:25,099 --> 00:01:37,161
And it's a Mono build, not IL2CPP. That matters here.
On IL2CPP I have to recover the package list from leftover filenames. On Mono the assemblies are just there.

12
00:01:37,411 --> 00:01:45,554
So for once this is the real list, not my reconstruction of one.
A hundred and eighty two DLLs. And three of them stopped me.

13
00:01:45,804 --> 00:01:54,418
MCPForUnity dot Runtime. That's the Model Context Protocol bridge,
the thing that lets an AI agent drive the Unity editor.

14
00:01:54,668 --> 00:02:03,883
Next to it, Unity dot AI dot MCP dot Runtime. That's Unity's own.
Both are in the same build, from the same folder.

15
00:02:04,133 --> 00:02:12,433
Then Unity's Inference Engine, with a tokenization assembly beside it.
A tokenizer is text model tooling. It isn't there to sharpen textures.

16
00:02:12,683 --> 00:02:18,005
And thirteen megabytes of DirectML,
Microsoft's GPU inference runtime.

17
00:02:18,255 --> 00:02:28,175
Here's what that does and doesn't mean. MCP is an editor tool.
Finding it in a player build tells you it wasn't stripped out, not that the game is talking to an agent while you play.

18
00:02:28,425 --> 00:02:38,397
What it does tell you is that this game was built with an AI agent wired into the editor,
and the wiring is still visible from outside. That's the first time I've been able to see it in a file list.

19
00:02:38,647 --> 00:02:42,533
Once you know nothing was stripped,
the rest of the list reads differently.

20
00:02:42,783 --> 00:02:54,897
Better Inspector and Better Mesh are Asset Store editor tools. Unity Recorder captures video in the editor.
Six Timeline sample assemblies, and a documentation examples assembly.

21
00:02:55,147 --> 00:03:06,974
There are also two ASP dot NET web pages in there, one for Mono two point zero and one for four point zero.
Those ship with the stock Mono tree. Nobody put them there on purpose.

22
00:03:07,224 --> 00:03:10,509
Now the size,
because it's the number you can act on.

23
00:03:10,759 --> 00:03:19,791
Four point four three gigabytes of the six are resS files.
That's Unity's raw texture and audio stream. Seventy three percent of the download.

24
00:03:20,041 --> 00:03:27,871
And Steam still finds forty percent to compress out of the finished package.
That's what an uncrunched texture set looks like from the outside.

25
00:03:28,121 --> 00:03:33,992
Reception, then. There isn't any.
No reviews, a handful of players, one day old.

26
00:03:34,242 --> 00:03:43,927
So I'll say the honest thing instead. The trailer is very dark,
and the demo is a small studio's first swing at a location every Indian ghost story already knows.

27
00:03:44,177 --> 00:03:46,678
Here's the whole teardown on one card.

28
00:03:46,928 --> 00:03:54,627
Unity 6 on HDRP, Mono, six gigabytes,
two MCP runtimes, an inference engine and a tokenizer.

29
00:03:54,877 --> 00:03:59,598
Worth a dip,
if you like slow first-person horror and you can stand how dark it is.

30
00:03:59,848 --> 00:04:11,544
If you build in Unity, the thing to take from this is the strip list. Open your player build and search it for Recorder,
for editor inspectors, for anything with MCP in the name. If it's here, it shipped.

31
00:04:11,794 --> 00:04:22,550
That's my read from the outside. If you worked on this and I got something wrong,
say so and I'll pin the correction. Next time, another demo, another file list. This is Demo Dip.
